/*
 * Aggregates all visitor modules involved in the syntax pass of the compiler.
 *
 * The syntax visitor subsystem is responsible for transforming raw source text
 * into a structured syntax tree. Each submodule implements a specialized
 * visitor for a specific syntactic construct(declarations, expressions,
 * templates, attributes, etc.), while `SyntaxVisitor` orchestrates the parsing
 * process and drives the lexer.
 *
 * This file exposes the public entry point of the syntax pass and groups all
 * grammar-level visitors into a single namespace.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::syntax::visitor
 * @File: ymirc/syntax/visitor.yr
 * @Author(s):
